ese Lewis George was elected mayor on November 3 and takes office January 2, 2027.","source":"https://www.fox5dc.com/news/dc-mayor-elect-janeese-lewis-george-names-transition-team"}},{"office":"Attorney General","name":"Brian L. Schwalb","url":"https://oag.dc.gov/"}],"statewideTerm":"The District of Columbia has no governor or lieutenant governor: its mayor and attorney general are the elected executive officers, and its legislature is the 13-member Council. A general election was held on November 3, 2026: Janeese Lewis George (now Ward 4's councilmember) was elected mayor and Brian Schwalb was reelected attorney general; officials elected then take office on January 2, 2027, and the Council seats up (including Ward 4's, to be filled by a special election) are not changed in this list yet.","notes":{"election":"A general election was held on November 3, 2026. This list shows officials in office on the build date; people elected on November 3 take office on January 2, 2027 (D.C. elected a new delegate, Robert White, and a new mayor). The District has no U.S. senators; it elects one non-voting delegate to the House. Its \"shadow\" senators and representative are not listed.","transition":"D.C.'s November 3 results are unofficial until the Board of Elections certifies them (scheduled for December 2, 2026). A new mayor, a new delegate and two new councilmembers were elected; they take office in January 2027. This was D.C.'s first ranked-choice election for Council seats.","transitionSource":"https://electionresults.dcboe.org/"},"districtNames":{"house":{},"senate":{"1":"Ward 1","2":"Ward 2","3":"Ward 3","4":"Ward 4","5":"Ward 5","6":"Ward 6","7":"Ward 7","8":"Ward 8"}},"titles":{"upper":"Councilmember","legislature":"Council of the District of Columbia","delegate":"Delegate"}}